  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 370,
   "y": 370,
   "width": 592,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100040,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700280,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Lookup: binary search for the largest entry <= target, then SCAN FORWARD\ninside a 4 KB window. One index lookup plus one short sequential read.\n\nA 1 GB segment of 1 KB messages holds ~1 million messages. Indexing every\none costs ~8 MB of index per GB and turns index lookups into their own\nrandom-read problem. Sparse costs ~16 KB/GB - small enough to mmap and\neffectively always resident.",
   "originalText": "Lookup: binary search for the largest entry <= target, then SCAN FORWARD\ninside a 4 KB window. One index lookup plus one short sequential read.\n\nA 1 GB segment of 1 KB messages holds ~1 million messages. Indexing every\none costs ~8 MB of index per GB and turns index lookups into their own\nrandom-read problem. Sparse costs ~16 KB/GB - small enough to mmap and\neffectively always resident.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bp",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 370,
   "y": 508,
   "width": 264,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100041,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700287,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The principle worth extracting",
   "originalText": "The principle worth extracting",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bp2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 370,
   "y": 534,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100042,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700294,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A sparse index trades a BOUNDED SEQUENTIAL SCAN for a large reduction in index size. Sequential\nscanning is nearly free here (244x), so spending a 4 KB scan to save 500x on index size is obviously\nright. In a random-access system the same trade would be wrong. Index density is a function of how\ncheap your scan is.",
   "originalText": "A sparse index trades a BOUNDED SEQUENTIAL SCAN for a large reduction in index size. Sequential\nscanning is nearly free here (244x), so spending a 4 KB scan to save 500x on index size is obviously\nright. In a random-access system the same trade would be wrong. Index density is a function of how\ncheap your scan is.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
