   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "linger_ms = 0    ->  lowest latency, smallest batches, lowest throughput\nlinger_ms = 100  ->  highest throughput, +100ms at p99",
   "originalText": "linger_ms = 0    ->  lowest latency, smallest batches, lowest throughput\nlinger_ms = 100  ->  highest throughput, +100ms at p99",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "dial",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dialn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 810,
   "y": 796,
   "width": 689,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "This is exactly how the 'configurable latency versus throughput' requirement is met:\nthe same code serves a 5ms order pipeline and a 500 MB/sec log aggregator by changing\none number. And it is why a routing tier was rejected - a middle tier never sees one\nproducer's messages for one partition together, so it cannot batch them at all.",
   "originalText": "This is exactly how the 'configurable latency versus throughput' requirement is met:\nthe same code serves a 5ms order pipeline and a 500 MB/sec log aggregator by changing\none number. And it is why a routing tier was rejected - a middle tier never sees one\nproducer's messages for one partition together, so it cannot batch them at all.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
